**Excerpt from Manufacturing and Distribution Agreement**

**Clause 5: Safety and Compliance Standards**  
5.1 The Manufacturer, ABC Manufacturing Co., located at 123 Industrial Way, Springfield, IL, hereby agrees to adhere to all applicable safety regulations as outlined by the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standards, specifically 29 CFR 1910, and any other relevant local, state, or federal laws. Compliance shall be verified through quarterly audits conducted by Safety Solutions LLC, an independent safety compliance auditor.

5.2 The Manufacturer shall ensure that all employees are trained in the proper handling of materials, as well as emergency response protocols, with training certifications provided to XYZ Distribution Inc., located at 456 Logistics Blvd, Chicago, IL, within 30 days of completion. Non-compliance with training requirements may result in a suspension of distribution activities until rectifications are made.

**Clause 6: Packaging Requirements**  
6.1 All products manufactured shall be packaged in accordance with the specifications outlined in Exhibit A of this Agreement, which includes the use of biodegradable materials and adherence to the labeling standards set forth by the Federal Trade Commission (FTC). Packaging processes shall be documented and submitted for review by XYZ Distribution Inc. to ensure readiness for transportation and shelf display.

6.2 ABC Manufacturing Co. shall implement a quality control process that includes a minimum of three inspections per production batch, with detailed reports sent to XYZ Distribution Inc. within 48 hours of inspection completion. Failure to meet packaging standards may result in penalties as described in Clause 8.

**Clause 7: Distribution Responsibilities**  
7.1 XYZ Distribution Inc. shall be responsible for the logistics and distribution of all finished goods manufactured by ABC Manufacturing Co. to retail locations as specified in Schedule B. The Manufacturer agrees to provide a shipping schedule at least two weeks in advance to facilitate the timely processing of orders.

7.2 Should any product recall be necessitated by safety or compliance failures, the Manufacturer shall bear all costs associated with the recall process, including transportation and disposal of affected products, and shall immediately notify XYZ Distribution Inc. to coordinate the response plan. 

This Agreement shall remain in effect until terminated by either party with a written notice of 60 days, or until a breach of these clauses occurs, at which point remediation must be attempted prior to termination.